{%- comment -%}
  ═══ LBASS — CAMPAIGN ELIGIBILITY TEST (2026-09-09). Echoes "1" or "0". ═══

  SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for "is this product in the running promotion".
  Every promotional surface in the theme asks THIS file and nothing else.

  ── WHAT THE CAMPAIGN ACTUALLY IS ────────────────────────────────────────────
  «‑30% على القطعة الثانية» — a real Shopify AUTOMATIC Buy-X-Get-Y discount.
  The customer buys two eligible pieces and the cheaper one is 30% off at
  checkout. Shopify applies it; the theme only announces it.

  THE ITEM'S OWN PRICE IS NOT REDUCED. That is the whole point of choosing this
  mechanism, and it dictates how the badge may be worded:

      ALLOWED   «‑30% على الثانية»     — true, the 2nd item is 30% off
      BANNED    «‑30%» on its own      — reads as "this item is 30% off". It is not.
      BANNED    any strikethrough price driven by this campaign

  A struck-through price on a card may ONLY come from a genuine Shopify
  `compare_at_price` (see snippets/lbass-price.liquid). The campaign never
  fabricates one. templates/product.liquid:700 already states the rule this
  file obeys: a figure that was never our price is misrepresentation and risks
  the Merchant Center listings.

  ── WHY A TAG AND NOT A METAFIELD ────────────────────────────────────────────
  The badge and the discount MUST cover exactly the same products, or the page
  promises something checkout does not honour. Only a tag can drive all three
  consumers at once:

      tag `summer-sale`
        ├─ smart collection `summer-sale`   (auto-updating, tag rule)
        ├─ the automatic discount            (scoped to that collection)
        └─ this file                         (product.tags contains …)

  `lbass.promo_eligible` stays what it always was: the editorial "may this piece
  be promoted at all" flag. The tag is the mechanical switch. Both must agree —
  this file requires the tag and treats promo_eligible as a veto, so clearing
  either one removes the product from the campaign.

  ── AVAILABILITY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Sold-out pieces never carry the badge. Everything here is one-of-one, so a
  sold piece can never be the second item in anyone's basket. Announcing an
  offer on it is a dead promise.

  ── OFF BY DEFAULT ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  `settings.promo_enabled` is nil until config/settings_schema.json ships, and
  nil is falsy, so the campaign renders nothing until a human switches it on in
  the theme editor. That is the intended failure mode.

  USAGE — render returns a string, so capture and strip it:

      {% capture promo_s %}{% render 'lbass-promo', product: product %}{% endcapture %}
      {% assign promo_s = promo_s | strip %}
      {% assign is_promo = false %}{% if promo_s == '1' %}{% assign is_promo = true %}{% endif %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign lb_promo_on = false

  if settings.promo_enabled and product != blank
    assign lb_tag = settings.promo_tag | default: 'summer-sale' | downcase | strip

    comment
      Case-insensitive tag match. The catalogue mixes "black" and "Black", so
      never compare product.tags directly — build a lowercased CSV index first.
    endcomment
    assign lb_index = ','
    for t in product.tags
      comment
        Normalise EACH tag before appending. Chaining `| downcase | strip` onto
        the accumulator instead would strip only the ends of the whole string,
        so a tag stored as " summer-sale " kept its inner spaces and never
        matched. Caught by the render harness 2026-09-09.
      endcomment
      assign lb_t = t | downcase | strip
      assign lb_index = lb_index | append: lb_t | append: ','
    endfor
    assign lb_needle = ',' | append: lb_tag | append: ','

    if lb_index contains lb_needle
      if product.available
        comment
          Editorial veto. Only an explicit `false` removes the piece; an unset
          metafield leaves the tag in charge, so newly added stock that carries
          the tag is not silently dropped from the campaign.
        endcomment
        unless product.metafields.lbass.promo_eligible.value == false
          assign lb_promo_on = true
        endunless
      endif
    endif
  endif

  if lb_promo_on
    echo '1'
  else
    echo '0'
  endif
-%}
